  "purpose": "Evaluate one bounded NSESche mechanism repair on fresh E713-E715 development seeds for all three E3 burst scenarios and E4 steady balanced-QoS, while reusing the sealed V87 advanced-baseline cohort without any baseline rerun.",
  "first_principles_hypothesis": {
    "observed_V87_failure": "V87 terminal-OCS candidates used a parents-completed ready frontier and did not persist both OCS affinity and FaaSRank diversity histories across windows. In E3, approximately 95.3%-96.9% of window-safe proposals fell back, mostly because paper welfare was not strictly improved, while the actually scheduled player count was far below pending request-function observations.",
    "bounded_repair": "Use the dependency-pipeline parents-scheduled frontier, retain native FaaSRank request/DAG order, route terminal functions through the exact OCS proxy and nonterminal functions through faithful FaaSRank, preserve both expert histories across windows, and retain the dual-expert plus paper-welfare atomic certificate.",
    "expected_effect": "Expose more schedulable work without changing the paper welfare definition, improve terminal throughput through OCS affinity continuity, and protect QPR through FaaSRank diversity continuity and the unchanged window-safe certificate.",
    "not_a_scaling_change": true
  },
